# Nura brand

Full spec: [`docs/brand.md`](docs/brand.md). Constants: [`lib/brand.ts`](lib/brand.ts). Logo: [`BrandLockup`](app/components/BrandLockup.tsx).

## Name

**Say and write Nura. URL is nurahelp.com (domain only).** Operator: **Receptly LLC** (`lib/legal-entity.ts`).

| Layer | Name | Where |
|---|---|---|
| Brand / chrome | Nura | Sidebar, headers, email from-name, Stripe Checkout, WebAuthn `rpName`, lockup |
| Legal operator | Receptly LLC | Terms, Privacy, JSON-LD `legalName` |
| Marketing footer line | © {year} Nura \| All rights reserved | Site footer only — operator stays on legal pages |
| Product feature | EMDR Support | Not the company name |
| Never in public | NuraHelp / NuraHelp AI | Domain host only — rewrite leftovers via `rewriteRetiredBrandCopy` |

```ts
// ❌ BAD
"NuraHelp"
"NuraHelp AI"
"Nura Help"

// ✅ GOOD
import { BRAND_SPOKEN } from "@/lib/brand";
import { legalEntityDisplayName } from "@/lib/legal-entity";
chromeBrandName(raw) // maps leftover "NuraHelp" → Nura
rewriteRetiredBrandCopy(text) // stored help/knowledge copy
```

Leading with “AI” is allowed for the product itself — Nura is **AI-guided EMDR**, so titles, hero, and H1s may say **AI-guided EMDR** / **AI guided EMDR session** (it is the position and the search term). The **wordmark and brand name stay “Nura”** — never “Nura AI”, “NuraHelp AI”, or an AI-prefixed logo. Do not invent a new logo — use `BrandLockup` with the wave wordmark (`tone="color" | "black" | "white"`; `href` defaults to `null`; wrap in `Link` or pass `href`). Admin lockup → `/admin`. Assets: `public/brand/nura-wave-logo*.png`, mark/favicon under `public/brand/` + `app/icon.svg`.

## Position

Calm guided therapy support — EMDR and resources in the app. Not an AI therapist, EHR, or emergency care. Marketing disclaimer: self-help, not a licensed therapist. No “find a therapist” / human matching — product is app-only.

Hero: **EMDR therapy online.** *in a calm app.* (tagline still: Support for therapy. Starting with EMDR.)

## Visual

- Pistachio palette: Paper/mint `#A4EDA5` · Sage `#84B067` (buttons, wordmark) · Ink `#2A3020` (body) · Pistachio `#C6D67E` **focus/hover only, never body or default field borders** · Olive `#948F4E` (muted) · Sidebar `#3D4129`
- Forbidden: OpenAI `#10a37f`, Apple `#007AFF`, Inter, purple wellness, hospital blue
- **Product type** (`/app`, `.app-shell`, `.auth-shell`): **Source Sans 3 only** — remaps `--font-display` to sans (same idea as admin). No Fraunces in product chrome or auth titles.
- **Admin type** (`/admin`, `.admin-shell`): **Source Sans 3 only** — sober UI; remaps `--font-display` to `--font-sans` so titles/KPIs are not ornamental Fraunces
- **Marketing type** (`.frontend-home`): Fraunces **only** on the **home hero** title (decorative). Everywhere else on marketing — section titles, pricing, how-it-works, blog cards, FAQ — **Source Sans 3**. **Blog, Learn, articles, About/EMDR hubs, and legal** use Source Sans 3 for h1–h3 (weight 600). See **Frontend typography** below.
- Tokens live in `app/globals.css`. Marketing uses `.frontend-home`; product UI uses product tokens (see `product-ui` rule)

## Frontend typography (aligned with product)

Loaded via `next/font` in `app/layout.tsx`. Scoped on `.frontend-home` in `app/globals.css`.

| Role | Font | CSS var | Where |
|---|---|---|---|
| Marketing **home hero** title only | **Fraunces** (400; italic for emphasis) | `--font-display` → `--font-fraunces` | Home hero display title only — not pricing, how-it-works, blog, FAQ, or other sections |
| Blog / Learn / articles / legal / long-form / other marketing headings | **Source Sans 3** (headings 600) | `--font-sans` | `/blog`, `/learn`, landing sections, `/about`, `/emdr`, `/terms`, `/privacy` — never Fraunces |
| Body / UI | **Source Sans 3** | `--font-sans` | Paragraphs, nav, buttons, intro lead |
| Labels / kickers | **Roboto Mono** (400) | `--font-alt` → `--font-fe-alt` | `.fe-eyebrow`, `.fe-section-kicker`, marquee — uppercase, ~0.9375rem |

**Rules:**
- Marketing **home hero** title: Fraunces weight **400**; all other marketing headings + legal: Source Sans **600**
- Heading/body **line-height 1.2** on marketing heroes; legal/long paragraphs ~1.5–1.6
- Kickers: mono, uppercase, muted color — never bold sans competing with the lockup
- Marketing and product share one voice; do **not** use Inter or soft rounded grotesks (retired: Libre Caslon Condensed, BDOGrotesk)
- Scale (desktop marketing): h1 ~4rem, h2 ~3rem, h3 ~2.5rem, body lead ~1.25rem, body sm ~1–1.1rem, xs ~0.9375rem (readable chrome floor ~12px). Legal page titles stay ~1.75rem / section ~1.125rem.

**Header (pill nav):** floating `frontend-header-pill` — logo | center nav **Home · How it works · Prices · Blog · FAQ** (hash links on `/`) | guests: **Sign in** + **Get started** pill; signed-in: name + avatar dropdown. No auth links in center nav. Styles: `frontend-header.css`.

## Copy

English, sentence case, short. No hype (“revolutionary”, “blockchain”, “neural networks”).

### Never use the em dash (—)

The long dash `—` (U+2014) in the middle of a sentence reads as AI-written. **Do not use it in user-facing copy** (UI, agent lines, emails, help, FAQ, marketing body, onboarding). Prefer a comma, period, colon, or parentheses.

```txt
# ❌ BAD
Welcome. In a few words — what would you like to work on today?
Animation, sound, and joystick rumble — you set speed and timing.

# ✅ GOOD
Welcome. In a few words, what would you like to work on today?
Animation, sound, and joystick rumble. You set speed and timing.
```

Also strip `—` from agent/system prompts that shape spoken or chat lines (`lib/protocol.ts`, `lib/protocol-knowledge.ts`), or the model will keep writing them.

OK elsewhere: code comments, Cursor rules/docs for agents, and the layout title template ` — Nura` / existing SEO title stems (prefer `:` when writing new titles).

**Marketing:** do not explain the product in body paragraphs — titles, labels, cards, and visuals do the work (see `.cursor/rules/marketing-no-explain-copy.mdc`). Product/auth/onboarding may use short microcopy where needed.

### Never say BLS to users

**BLS** (bilateral stimulation) is internal jargon. Do **not** put it in UI, emails, help, onboarding, billing, upgrade modals, status chips, marketing, or admin copy that users might see.

| Instead of | Write |
|---|---|
| BLS / free BLS / BLS minutes | **self-guided set time** / **set time** |
| BLS running | **Set running** |
| BLS bar / BLS controls | **Controls bar** / **Session controls** |
| BLS preview | **self-guided set time** (or “live preview” for the gear sheet) |

Code/CSS identifiers may stay (`bls`, `TRIAL_BLS_SECONDS`, `.bls-dock`) — that is not user-facing. Extend `rewriteRetiredBrandCopy` if remapping stored help text.

### Visual sets — do not default to “moving ball”

Self-guided / AI agent-guided sets are **not** “just a ball.” The product already has multiple stimulus options (e.g. Dot and Flash animations, stereo sound, gamepad rumble), and more will ship. Marketing and first-run copy must not collapse the product to one animation.

| Instead of (default) | Write |
|---|---|
| the moving ball / just the ball | **visual set** / **sets** / **session sets** |
| Free is the moving ball only | **Self-guided is sets you run yourself** (no agent, no chat) |
| BLS controls → moving ball | **Session controls** (speed, animation, sound, repeats) |

OK to name the ball **once** on educational pages (`/emdr`, a guide about visual rhythm) as *one* way the set can look — not as the product definition, and not in Self-guided headlines (“The moving ball, on your terms” is banned).

### Session modes (marketing + first-run copy)

See `.cursor/rules/session-mode-names.mdc`. Never use bare **“Choose Guided or Free”** — and never name the self-run mode **Free session** (reads as $0).

| Instead of | Write |
|---|---|
| Guided / Guided mode / Agent-guided | **AI agent-guided** / **AI agent-guided session** / **session agent** |
| Free mode / Free session | **Self-guided** / **Self-guided session** (sets you run yourself) |
| Choose Guided or Free | **Choose AI agent-guided or Self-guided** — then one line: agent walks phases; Self-guided is sets without an agent |

Product chrome labels: **AI agent-guided session** · **Self-guided session**. Headlines **may** lead with **AI-guided EMDR** (product + search term). Do not turn the wordmark into “Nura AI”. Internal code may stay `guided` / `free`.

Do **not** keep **Free session** in admin chrome either — operators copy that language into the product.

### Session language (AI agent-guided)

The guide mirrors the person, not the other way round. `lib/session-languages.ts` owns the language pack; `app/components/useRotatingWelcome.ts` owns the rotation.

| Rule | Detail |
|---|---|
| First line rotates | The opening welcome cycles through the major languages (~2.4s each) until the person writes. **No language name, code, or flag is shown**, only the greeting text |
| Locks on first writing | As soon as the composer draft or the first user message is recognizable, the greeting locks to that language (`detectSessionLanguage`) and stops rotating |
| Guide follows the user | `/api/chat` pins `threads.agent_language` and adds the language block to the system prompt: the guide replies in the user's language, including the post-set check-in |
| App chrome stays English | Buttons, chips, placeholders, phase labels, SUDs/VoC scales, and admin stay English. Only the guide's spoken lines are localized |
| Detection misses are safe | Unsure means English. Never guess a language from one ambiguous short word |

When adding a language: add an entry to `SESSION_LANGUAGES` (code, name, native, welcome, optional Latin hints, no em dash, no **BLS**) and extend `tests/session-languages.test.ts`.

Public routes (must stay in `lib/public-paths.ts` + `app/robots.txt/route.ts` + `app/sitemap.ts`): `/` `/about` `/editorial` `/emdr` `/learn` `/knowledge` `/blog` `/blog/[slug]` `/pricing` `/faq` `/support` `/changelog` `/privacy` `/terms` `/safety` `/limits`. Also public: `/llms.txt`. Nav: **Home · How it works · Prices · Blog · FAQ** (`Prices` → `/pricing`, `Blog` → `/blog`, `FAQ` → `/faq`; How it works stays `/#how-it-works`). No visible breadcrumbs on inner pages (JSON-LD BreadcrumbList may remain). Retired: `/therapy`, `/therapists`, and `/resources` redirect to `/learn`. In-app library stays `/app/resources`.
